# Records whose primary constructor may change in this PR.
#
# An entry is a STATEMENT THAT THE ATOMIC MOVE IS PLANNED — every bundle rebuilt and
# republished for the new signature, then the image rolled — not a way to make the gate quiet.
# There is no image that can serve a mixed set of module builds: a consumer compiled against
# the old arity aborts the host at boot, in both directions.
#
# One fully-qualified type per line, then the PULL REQUEST this entry travels with, then a
# reason:
#
#   BurstAggregation  #2234 — bundles republished in the same wave, image rolled after
#
# 🚨 AN ENTRY IS TRANSITIONAL AND EXPIRES BY MECHANISM, not by anyone remembering (#3422).
#
#   * It is in force ONLY in the diff that ADDS it. The moment it merges, the line stops being
#     an addition, and every later pull request treats it as INERT: it permits nothing, and it
#     fails nothing. There is nothing here for you to delete on a later day — deleting a landed
#     line is tidying, never a fix.
#   * The `#<number>` is a PULL REQUEST in this repository and the gate resolves it. Open, and
#     the allowance stands. Merged, closed-unmerged, an issue, missing, or unresolvable, and the
#     gate goes RED naming which: "could not tell" never renders as "allowed".
#   * An entry that permits nothing in the diff that adds it still FAILS — on that diff, which
#     is its author's own pull request.
#
# The line this replaces read "DELETE the line once the change has shipped". Nobody did, once;
# for ~40 minutes every C#-touching pull request in the fleet was red on somebody else's merge.
# See Doc/Architecture/TransitionalAllowEntries.
PrebuiltBundleSweepPlan  #3749 — the record shipped in #3741 hours earlier and is in no released image or module; 2 references org-wide, both core (definition + its test); no in-mesh source names it
RailGroup  #4321 — SuppliedNavigationRail.RailGroup: parameter 4 Links (IReadOnlyList<RailLink>) becomes Items (IReadOnlyList<RailItem>) so a group can nest a group; constructed ONLY by core (SuppliedNavigationRail.Plan) — no compiled module, no in-mesh source and no satellite constructs it (grep across Plugins, SocialMedia, Reinsurance, Manufacturing, Education: Edu consumes NodeNavigation, never RailGroup); Links stays as a read-only filter property
TypeBuild  #4739 — CascadeBuild.TypeBuild lives in tools/MeshWeaver.PluginTester, which is OutputType=Exe with AssemblyName=mw-plugin-test: a CLI that ships as ONE unit inside the tester image, loaded by no portal and compiled against by no module, so there is no mixed set to serve. Consumers measured rather than assumed: 2, both in this repository (the record's own file and test/MeshWeaver.PluginTester.Test/StaticTestRunnerTest.cs), both updated in this same diff; no .csproj in MeshWeaver.Plugins, .Education, .Reinsurance or .SocialMedia references the tester, and no in-mesh source names the type. The member removed (BindsDependencyAssemblies) is retired with the dependency-assembly references themselves.
